.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt SYSTEM_PROFILER 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm system_profiler
.Nd report the system's hardware and software configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl listDataTypes
.Nm
.Op Fl xml | Fl json
.Op Fl detailLevel Ar mini | basic | full
.Op Fl timeout Ar seconds
.Op Ar dataType ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reports the configuration of the machine by data type.
Without a data type it reports all of them; a data type it does not know
is not reported.
The data types are:
.Bl -tag -width SPHardwareDataType
.It Cm SPHardwareDataType
The model, the processors and their caches, the memory, the firmware
version, the serial number and the hardware UUID.
.It Cm SPNetworkDataType
Each Ethernet interface: its BSD name, IPv4 addresses and subnet masks,
MAC address and media.
.It Cm SPSoftwareDataType
The system and kernel versions, the boot volume and mode, the computer and
user names, whether swap is encrypted, System Integrity Protection and the
time since boot.
.It Cm SPStorageDataType
Each mounted local volume: free space and capacity, mount point, file
system, whether it is writable and ignores ownership, its BSD name and
UUID, and the drive it is on (name, medium, protocol, whether internal, and
the partition map).
.El
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl listDataTypes
List the data types and exit.
.It Fl xml
Report as a property list: an array with a dictionary per data type, its
items under
.Li _items .
.It Fl json
Report as JSON: an object with an array of items per data type.
.It Fl detailLevel Ar level
.Ar mini
leaves out what identifies the machine or its user (serial number, UUIDs,
computer and user names, MAC addresses);
.Ar basic
and
.Ar full ,
the default, report everything.
.It Fl timeout Ar seconds
Accepted for compatibility; nothing is waited for.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr ioreg 8 ,
.Xr sw_vers 1 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
